{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1088995-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-the-curse","id":1088995,"title":"Ask a simple question, get a simple answer: Mummy The Curse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-06T21:21:40-07:00","id":1088995,"title":"Ask a simple question, get a simple answer: Mummy The Curse","content":"I didn't see this thread in the forum, so I figured I'd make it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Please correct me If I'm mistaken and this thread already in existence for Mummy.<br /> <br /> Question: Do Utterances have a flat dice pool? If it's not stated - does it not have a dice pool for it? For example like <i>Tier 2 of Word of the Amanuesis</i>. I know some abilities don't have them but it seems a lot of them are missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T22:12:35-07:00","id":1089005,"title":"","content":"Utterances have no standard dice pool mechanic. This is intentional. The design team wanted some Utterances to always work, others to have a dice pool that scales with Sekhem, and others to have a dice pool that didn't scale at all. Some Utterances were meant to emphasise the descent by declining in power as the Mummy did, while others were intended to remain at the same strength until the Arisen lost access to them entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T01:32:14-07:00","id":1089043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1088995-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-the-curse?p=1089005#post1089005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Utterances have no standard dice pool mechanic. This is intentional. The design team wanted some Utterances to always work, others to have a dice pool that scales with Sekhem, and others to have a dice pool that didn't scale at all. Some Utterances were meant to emphasise the descent by declining in power as the Mummy did, while others were intended to remain at the same strength until the Arisen lost access to them entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in regards to Tier 2 - Word of Amaunuesis; does this roll sybaris or the like? Or if a power clashes against it - is it a clash of wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T03:09:48-07:00","id":1089052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1088995-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-the-curse?p=1089043#post1089043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in regards to Tier 2 - Word of Amaunuesis; does this roll sybaris or the like? Or if a power clashes against it - is it a clash of wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Mummy actually predates the Clash of Wills rule I think, so any clash would come down to GM fiat in all likelihood. Which could well mean a clash of wills if you're that way inclined.<br /> <br /> With respect to Tier 2, I'm not sure what you mean exactly? The Tier 2 provides a benefit to all rolls to Intimidate, and an additional bonus to rolls against those suffering from Sybaris. If the target is suffering from Sybaris, they can ignore their Sybaris for the duration of carrying out the Mummy's orders. For the most part it just modifies other actions. Which part of it do you feel requires a dice roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:51:24-07:00","id":1089150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1088995-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-the-curse?p=1089052#post1089052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Mummy actually predates the Clash of Wills rule I think, so any clash would come down to GM fiat in all likelihood. Which could well mean a clash of wills if you're that way inclined.<br /> <br /> With respect to Tier 2, I'm not sure what you mean exactly? The Tier 2 provides a benefit to all rolls to Intimidate, and an additional bonus to rolls against those suffering from Sybaris. If the target is suffering from Sybaris, they can ignore their Sybaris for the duration of carrying out the Mummy's orders. For the most part it just modifies other actions. Which part of it do you feel requires a dice roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind - It was late last night and I misread it - Apologies * thanks for the help Azahul <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T13:48:34-07:00","id":1134244,"title":"","content":"So under the Mesen-Nebu stereotypes, we have:<br /> <br /> &quot;Su-Menent: I appreciate physicality as much as the next woman, but to paraphrase, if you like it then you should put a ring on it. A gold one, with certain properties.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are lots of things that I don't understand about <i>Mummy</i>, but this one stands out to me, because I infer from it that Merew-Tjaw has been listening to <i>Single Ladies</i> by Beyonce. But what else does it mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T14:39:56-07:00","id":1134259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1088995-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-the-curse?p=1134244#post1134244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So under the Mesen-Nebu stereotypes, we have:<br /> <br /> &quot;Su-Menent: I appreciate physicality as much as the next woman, but to paraphrase, if you like it then you should put a ring on it. A gold one, with certain properties.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are lots of things that I don't understand about <i>Mummy</i>, but this one stands out to me, because I infer from it that Merew-Tjaw has been listening to <i>Single Ladies</i> by Beyonce. But what else does it mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed it was a dig, referencing the idea that the priesthood fiddles around with corpses, and Arisen are technically corpses, especially while in repose. I'dve said something more like ''if you're going to be fiddling around with my body, at least buy me dinner first''<br /> <br /> Of course, there are nuances. For one, Shellshepherds focus on the physical body, rather than the Dewdwen it contained. If focusing on the physical, at least focus on something beautiful like jewelry. Much prettier than corpses.<br /> <br /> Similarly, there are many things that the Su-Menent seem to flirt, or even obsess over, without ''committing'' to it. They fixate on death and corpses, but not enough to stay dead. They worship the Elder Gods and Judges, but also seem more afraid of them than other Arisen. They could've fully committed themselves to the physical body, but instead cheat on it with gods and ghosts. <br /> <br /> Plus, who knows, maybe there is an enchanted Regina ring that can not only resurrect a corpse as easily as Uter magic, but can make them dance in unison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T00:04:18-08:00","id":1181032,"title":"","content":"So in Dark Eras Companion, it talks a bit about mummies creating ghosts in the mummy vs mage crossover section, but I can't seem to figure out what mummy power actually creates ghosts per se. Summons them, turns them into revenants and intruders, etc... but the only power I saw that directly seems to turn a mortal into a ghost is when a big chthonian ghost eater dude kills someone.<br /> <br /> Is there a specific power for making a living or dead person into a ghost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T15:27:35-08:00","id":1181246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1088995-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-the-curse?p=1181032#post1181032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in Dark Eras Companion, it talks a bit about mummies creating ghosts in the mummy vs mage crossover section, but I can't seem to figure out what mummy power actually creates ghosts per se. Summons them, turns them into revenants and intruders, etc... but the only power I saw that directly seems to turn a mortal into a ghost is when a big chthonian ghost eater dude kills someone.<br /> <br /> Is there a specific power for making a living or dead person into a ghost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Punching them super hard?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T17:01:25-08:00","id":1181275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1088995-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-the-curse?p=1181246#post1181246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Punching them super hard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is There An Affinity For That?<br /> <br /> (I do have the humourous image of a mummy Falcon-Punching the ghost out of someone.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T15:19:36-08:00","id":1181508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1088995-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-the-curse?p=1181275#post1181275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is There An Affinity For That?<br /> <br /> (I do have the humourous image of a mummy Falcon-Punching the ghost out of someone.)</div> </div> </div> </div>For punching really hard? Guardian Wrath springs to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T15:58:00-08:00","id":1181511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1088995-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-the-curse?p=1181508#post1181508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For punching really hard? Guardian Wrath springs to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but unless I forget, it doesn't let you literally punch the ghost out of someone.<br /> <br /> A more &quot;gentle&quot; example:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kkVcsMZkP2k/maxresdefault.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T13:31:40-08:00","id":1184864,"title":"","content":"Can Mummies have children?<br /> <br /> Yes, no, or there's no mention either way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T13:55:22-08:00","id":1184879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1088995-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-the-curse?p=1184864#post1184864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Mummies have children?<br /> <br /> Yes, no, or there's no mention either way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, before they became mummies. No, after, as they are undead. The standard &quot;except with fertility magic because <i>magic</i>&quot; exception applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}